PROTOCOL_JSON {"stage": "hybrid F2-E", "scope": "CPU only: numpy and ORT's CPU EP; no NPU, no GPU", "pins": {"the F2 plan": {"file": "scratch/llm/hybrid_f2_plan_draft.md", "lf_sha256": "b98787f451c11fbc9e847a4cb973b8f12b4988e3dce7729435d1fd34334a07c5"}, "the F2-0b addendum": {"file": "scratch/llm/hybrid_f2_0b_addendum.md", "lf_sha256": "81dfe8da781aedd8513945c95b556739545326f80cda2b66fab0ba2504b3c26c"}, "the F2-E addendum": {"file": "scratch/llm/hybrid_f2e_addendum.md", "lf_sha256": "1ad61601f743525b6c08c2de38a86bad6f32f742e756a25333d5b257f2f165ec"}, "F2-0b's log": {"file": "results/llm/hybrid_f2_0b_desktop2_20260925.log", "lf_sha256": "dfd4849f5a7cbe8fe16ca39b69c9221a33333c682bd05b8588490eb9b371c4bf"}, "U6-E's run log": {"file": "results/llm/hybrid_u6e_run_desktop2_20260925.log", "lf_sha256": "adaa8fa8a1f4db89a85c30f49b3b48487a3fed28e494313efe4cecf5bbd07e4e"}, "f2_flush_b.cc": {"file": "kernels/f2_epilogue/f2_flush_b.cc", "lf_sha256": "caa62ce055f6e1a3e8de350349ac76bef3f8d9dd521416c9fb8db0c64a2e18d4"}, "the U6-E tool": {"file": "tools/hybrid_u6e.py", "lf_sha256": "b88d23d30c6c2ec3ffa55407dd4969957acf98e788fca47f1a703feec146e892"}, "the F2-0b tool": {"file": "tools/hybrid_f2_0b.py", "lf_sha256": "7a953146eaccc4b143bb4cf3072a84f10cad10f4f54bab1ec956d3588fcda354"}}, "layers": [0, 16, 33], "rows": {"count": 256, "first": 0, "last": 2040, "step": 8}, "arms": ["B/B2/ROW", "B/B2/16", "B/B2/8", "B/B3/ROW", "B/B3/16", "B/B3/8", "A/B2/ROW", "A/B2/16", "A/B2/8", "A/B3/ROW", "A/B3/16", "A/B3/8"], "deciding": ["B/B2/ROW", "B/B3/ROW"], "rule": "an arm (activation form, flush form, S) is ACCEPTABLE iff, for every case c (layers 0, 16 and 33 x the seven linears), r_F2(c) <= F2_FACTOR x r_R(c), with r_F2 = rel_l2(emulation, L0) and r_R = rel_l2(L4, L0) on the same 256 rows; F2_FACTOR = 2.0, deciding. The ACCEPTABLE set is printed at 1.12, 1.41 and 2.0", "f2_factor": 2.0, "factors": [1.12, 1.41, 2.0], "pick": "the pick is form B at S = ROW: FLUSH_B2 if ACCEPTABLE (E_F2 23.28125), else FLUSH_B3 (23.8125), else F2 SCREEN: NONE. A report-only arm (form A, or S = 16 or 8) is never picked; NONE ends F2 (plan section 6), and a pick opens F2-A only on the user's go", "a2": "A2-F2's threshold = up2(A2_FACTOR x the maximum over the 21 cases of rel_l2(emulation, F64_F2)) for the picked arm; the integer I must match exactly. NOT SET under NONE", "a2_factor": 2.0, "grid": "Sx = the smallest fp32 with 255 x Sx >= max s_x over the superblock, Dw the same with 127 x Dw >= max abs(d_w): the float64 quotient's fp32 round-up, then the exact float64 product check, stepping one ulp up where it fails. Form B: qx = max(1, c), c the exact ceiling of s_x / Sx (c = 256 is a STOP), codes RNE(x / (qx Sx)) in float64. Form A: L4's codes, qx = max(1, RNE(s_x / Sx)). qw = RNE(d_w / Dw). Any code or qw clip on real data is a STOP (the addendum, sections 1, 2.2 and 2.3)", "flush": "fp32(I) = RNE(I); per superblock in increasing K, y (fp32, from 0) takes one flush: split T of fp32(I), Sx and Dw (U6-E's split), P by ORDER P (a multiply, then fp32 adds of exact bf16 products), split T of P, then the ORDER Y terms added onto y. B3: T = 3, P and Y by ORDER[3]['P']; B2: T = 2, ORDER[2]['P'] and ORDER[2]['Y']", "orders": {"B3": {"P": [[3, 1], [2, 2], [1, 3], [2, 1], [1, 2], [1, 1]], "Y": [[3, 1], [2, 2], [1, 3], [2, 1], [1, 2], [1, 1]]}, "B2": {"P": [[2, 1], [1, 2], [1, 1]], "Y": [[2, 1], [1, 2], [1, 1]]}}, "e_f2": {"flush_pin": {"B2": 82, "B3": 116}, "e_core": 22, "row_blocks": 64, "rule": "E_F2 = E_core + FLUSH / row_blocks, exact; the log's 4-dp print must agree"}, "anchors": {"c2": "L4 on layer 16 equals S1's saved C2 output bit for bit, and reproduces C2's logged values (U6-E's anchor)", "u6e": "rel_l2(L4, L0) reproduces U6-E's logged l4_vs_l0 within 1e-06 relative"}, "b3_floor": "selftest: abs(B3 - F64) <= 8 x 2^-24 x abs(F64) per sample (DERIVED worst ~7.1)", "scope_note": "layer 16's activations only: x16_* on S1's sequence 0, rows 0, 8, ..., 2040, for all 21 cases; layers 0 and 33 use layer 16's activations (U6-E's assumption, hybrid_u6e.py:123)", "note_n2": "F2-E cannot change the N2 pick: F2's best modelled energy is 1.67x N-i8's measured energy (DECISIONS at ca75870); F2-E answers only whether F2's arithmetic is acceptable at S = ROW", "predictions": {"F2E-P1": "for each activation form and S, abs(r_F2(B2) - r_F2(B3)) <= 0.01 x r_R(c) in every case", "F2E-P2": "at ROW, form B's r_F2 <= form A's in every case, for both flush forms", "F2E-P3": "under form B, r_F2 does not increase as S shrinks (ROW, then 16, then 8), in every case, both flushes", "F2E-P4": "in each layer, down has the largest ROW qw = 0 fraction of the seven linears"}, "assumptions": ["AIE2's accfloat add rounds each MAC to fp32 by RNE, as numpy's float32 add does; SILICON does not record its rounding mode or denormal handling, and the scale products sit far above the denormal range", "the fp32 add at fp32(I)'s last step rounds to nearest even (INFERRED; the F2-0b addendum, section 1)", "a host reproduces the round-up of Sx and Dw and form B's float64 codes; a host rounding to nearest is not modelled"], "memory": "S1's start_gate: refuse below 15 GB available, and a watchdog ends the process below 5 GB; MEM_JSON last", "ort_version": "1.23.3.dev20260320"}
